<title>SPAIN: Spain's Q1 trade deficit fell by 22 percent.</title>
<headline>Spain's Q1 trade deficit fell by 22 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The customs department of the Economy Ministry gave the following figures (billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE		MARCH 97	FEB 97	 MARCH 96</p>
<p> Exports			1,291.9    1,079.2	   1,056.2</p>
<p> Imports			1,410.5    1,322.9	   1,249.6</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	     -118.7     -243.6	    -193.4</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date    -471.3     -358.8	    -604.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are customs-cleared data.  </p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE (EU)		 MAR 97	  FEB 97</p>
<p> Exports				 896.8	   773.5</p>
<p> Imports				 940.7	   872.0</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus		     -43.9	   -98.4</p>
<p> Def/surplus yr to date	   -130.0	   -59.0</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
